---
// Pearl › 06 — The Exception: an aside (label, italic quote, short accent rule) beside two
// italic paragraphs. Set in Google Sans Code italic on purpose (DESIGN.md › Google Sans Code).
// 80px band padding instead of 120. Figma's 32 line height on the paragraphs uses the
// pearl-quote token's 30.
import Section from './Section.astro';
---

<Section tone="white" width="wide" compact labelledby="exception-title">
  <div class="layout">
    <aside class="aside">
      <h2 class="text-label-s label" id="exception-title">one exception, early in the build</h2>
      <p class="text-pearl-quote quote">A quiet lesson about skipping the queue.</p>
      <span class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </aside>

    <div class="body text-pearl-quote text-body-l-mobile">
      <p>
        Two screens were built before Pearl was ready. While the foundations were still waiting
        on the client’s final colors, the Home Screen and My Plan wireframes were approved, and the
        UI was needed straight away. Home Screen made sense to do early. It set the visual
        direction everyone had to agree on, and after a few rounds of options, the client approved
        one. My Plan could have waited, but it went ahead too.
      </p>
      <p>
        The cost came later. When dark mode became urgent for the developers, both screens had to
        be rebuilt component by component, because they had never been built on the system in the
        first place. It was avoidable, and it’s the clearest reason I have to push back harder the
        next time a quick UI request tries to skip the system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  .layout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-64);
  }

  /* Figma gap 18, snapped to 16. Label and quote wrap at the 220 width, as in Figma. */
  .aside {
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    width: 220px;
  }

  .label {
    max-width: 120px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* The 16/24 pearl-quote size. */
  .quote {
    max-width: 200px;
    font-size: var(--body-l-size);
    line-height: var(--body-l-line);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .rule {
    width: 52px;
    height: 2px;
    background-color: var(--pearl-accent-line);
  }

  /* Figma gap 22, snapped to 24. */
  .body {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Tablet and mobile: the aside sits above the paragraphs. */
  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .layout {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-40);
    }
  }

  /* Mobile: 24 between the headline and the text, the same in every section (user). */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .layout {
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
